“application/json” is the correct mime type which is used to exchange the data in the format of key value pairs, between the applications.

Other options are not CORRECT because their functionality doesn’t match with the given requirement i.e. they can’t be used to send the response in the format of JSON (key value pairs).


The <head> element is a container for metadata. Metadata typically contains the document title, character set, styles, scripts, etc. The tags which can go inside <head> are, <title>, <style>, <base>, <link>, <meta>, <script>, <noscript>. So, <a> tag cannot be used inside head tag.

